{"study_accession":"PRJNA857311","secondary_study_accession":"SRP385714","title":"CD45 is sufficient to initiate EndMT in human endothelial cells","description":"Bulk RNA-Seq revealed that activation of the endogenous CD45 promoter induced expression of several genes implicated in EndMT. CD45-positive endothelial cells showed significantly increased migration, a hallmark of EndMT, increased collagen gel contraction, a hallmark of mesenchymal cells, and decreased cell-cell barrier integrity, indicating reduced endothelial function. Overall design: We activated the endogenous CD45 promoter in human endothelial colony forming cells (ECFCs) using a CRISPR/inactive Cas9 transcriptional activation system. Bulk RNA-Seq was carried out on control ECFCs and CD45-positive ECFCs (5 biological replicates for each) to identify transcriptomic changes.","pubmed":"36924233","geo_series":"","n_samples":10,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN29623559","study_accession":"PRJNA857311","blood_class":"cord_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Control ECFCs replicate 5","description":"Control ECFCs replicate 5","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6320885","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-06-05","attributes":[["source_name","umbilical cord blood"],["tissue","umbilical cord blood"],["cell_type","ECFC"],["genotype","WT"],["treatment","control"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR20071763","experiment_accession":"SRX16109799","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 4000","read_count":33961942,"base_count":10188582600,"first_public":"2023-06-05","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 4000 sequencing: GSM6320885: Control ECFCs replicate 5 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN29623560","study_accession":"PRJNA857311","blood_class":"cord_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Control ECFCs replicate 4","description":"Control